-- the argument list is a geometry and an optional properties tuple, so a third argument is rejected
-- at most four parameters are accepted
-- the first parameter (layer_name) must be a string
-- the second parameter (extent) must be an integer, and unsigned values outside [1, 2147483647] are rejected
-- a signed extent is held to the same range
-- the upper bound of the extent range is inclusive and both spellings encode the same tile
1
-- the third parameter (feature_id_name) must be a string
-- the fourth parameter (stringify_unsupported) must be an integer
-- any non-zero stringify_unsupported enables stringification, signed or unsigned alike
1
-- a signed zero leaves stringification off, so the Int128 property stays unsupported
